<title>HONG KONG: Trade in ONFEM, Oriental Metals suspended.</title>
<headline>Trade in ONFEM, Oriental Metals suspended.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in shares of ONFEM Holdings Ltd and Oriental Metals (Holdings) Co Ltd was suspended on Tuesday at the companies' request pending an announcement, the Hong Kong Stock Exchange said.  </p>
<p>On Monday, shares of property and industrial investment concern ONFEM rose HK$0.05 to end at HK$4.15.</p>
<p>Shares of Oriental Metals rose HK$0.12 to HK$1.64.</p>
<p>Oriental Metals is a metals trading firm authorised by state-owned China National Nonferrous Metals Industry Corp to engage in trading of non-ferrous metals.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
